    "lawCode": "Amd §13-0339-a, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7863A\n\nSPONSOR: BYNOE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nextending the authority of the department of environmental conservation\nto manage the American eel\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend the authority of the Department of\nEnvironmental Conservation (DEC) to manage American eel.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would extend, until December 31, 2026, DEC's authority to fix\nby regulation measures for the management of American eel.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhile the authority of DEC to manage American Eel is traditionally\nextended for three years, this bill would only extend such authority for\none year, given the recent classification of the American Eel as a\nspecies of concern by the DEC. Shortening such authorization will allow\nthe Legislature to evaluate DEC's current regulatory program for the\nAmerican Eel and work with the Department on changes in management prac-\ntices to bolster the species' population and develop strategies to help\nprevent it from becoming threatened or endangered in the future.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: Chapter 296.\n\n2019: Chapter 235.\n\n2016: Chapter 144.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
